{{!
    @template core/login_layout

    Richi Math override (MIG-21, 2026-10-09). New in 5.x: core splits every
    login-flow page (login, MFA…) in two, a decorative core/login_panel on the
    left and the form on the right. Our login already is a two-pane card of
    its own (Crystalline Academic Glass, core/loginform), so the split squeezed
    it into half the screen next to Moodle's promotional copy. This keeps a
    single full-width column. The ids are core's, so its JS still finds
    region-main and the login container; login-layout-right-content is left
    out on purpose, because core caps it at 576px for the right half.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * output - The core renderer output object (provides main_content).

    Example context (json):
    {
        "output": {
            "main_content": "<h1>Login form goes here</h1>"
        }
    }
}}
<div id="page-content" class="min-vh-100 row g-0">
    <div id="region-main" class="login-layout-right col-12">
        <div id="region-main-box">
            <div class="login-container">
                {{{ output.main_content }}}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
